{
    "background_story": "Aya was a brilliant and resourceful engineer who lived in a small village surrounded by lush forests and winding rivers. Growing up, she watched her father, a skilled carpenter, bring broken objects back to life with his skilled hands. Inspired by his handiness, Aya learned to fix and create just about anything. She could repair a leaky faucet, build a sturdy bookshelf, and even craft beautiful jewelry from scraps of metal and stone. When a devastating flood hit the village, Aya's handiness proved invaluable. She helped design and build makeshift shelters, repaired damaged bridges, and even created a system to purify contaminated water. Her ingenuity and skill earned her the nickname 'The Village MacGyver,' and she became a beloved and respected member of the community.",
